    "explanation": "Both of you agree the driver left the recommended route, and the record confirms it: the trip record logs a route_deviation_detected at 15:44:02 where the vehicle took Bukit Batok East Avenue 3 instead of the recommended Bukit Batok Road, and the driver-device trace puts the car on Bukit Batok East Avenue 3 and then Jurong Town Hall Road before it rejoined at Jurong East Street 21. The disagreement is over what follows from that.\n\nThe deviation is measured the way POL-RD-22 (Measuring the deviation) requires - from the platform's recorded distances, not by re-measuring the trace: actual 2.6 km minus recommended 2.2 km = 0.40 km. That sits below POL-RD-22's 1.0 km tolerance.\n\nPOL-RD-24 (Refund matrix) then applies exactly one row. The two rows for a deviation of 1 km or less - row (c) (traffic-justified, rider not informed) and row (e) (not traffic-justified) - both prescribe no refund. The LTA advisory for Bukit Batok Road (type NONE; no incident, roadwork or closure in the trip window) means the reroute was not traffic-justified, so row (e) applies: no refund, and the metered fare stands.\n\nTaking the rider's points in turn. It is correct that the reroute was not traffic-justified (POL-RD-23) and that the driver gave no notice - the chat log carries 0 messages and the trip record carries no in-app calls, so POL-RD-21's obligation was not met. But under POL-RD-24 the tolerance rows turn on the length of the deviation, not on justification or notice; notification is the concern of rows (a) and (b), which apply only where the deviation exceeds 1 km. For the same reason the rider's suggested 0.29 SGD does not arise: that is the excess-distance fare (0.40 km x 0.72 SGD on the fare breakdown), and POL-RD-24 uses it only in rows (b) and (d), each of which requires a deviation over 1 km. The 1.50 SGD originally claimed is likewise not a figure POL-RD-24 provides. Nor does POL-GEN-26 require escalation: the facts this case needs are on the record - the deviation distance is established at 0.40 km from the recorded distances, and the traffic data establishes the reroute was not justified - so there is no missing fact opening a question for a reviewer.\n\nThe record is complete, every artifact carries full admissibility weight 1.0, and the deviation is far below the 2.0 km limb that POL-RD-25 holds unapplied in this policy version, so an AI ruling properly stands (POL-GEN-22, dispute value 1.50 SGD, below the 10.00 SGD band).\n\nOutcome: the rider is owed nothing. The 1.50 SGD is not refunded and the fare stays as metered. This ruling is party-relative under POL-GEN-03 and leaves the present state in place; no referral is produced, as a route deviation carries no referral clause in this version.",
